"Kent Paul Dolan" <xanthian@well.com> writes:
[changing inventory icons in win32 graphical interface]

> I'm pretty sure the icons used in the menus are
> completely independent of the icons used on the map,
> since changing the map icons to the absurd tile set
> didn't modify the menu ones for me at all.

Right. The difference is between use of GetNHApp()->bmpTiles and
GetNHApp()->bmpMapTiles; _nethack_app.bmpMapTiles has been (possibly)
made different from the default-loaded _nethack_app.bmpTiles by
initMapTiles(). If your map tiles are the same size as the original
ones (16*16), then you may well just be able to change the reference
in onDrawItem() in win/win32/mhmenu.c from one to the other and have
it work (though I haven't tried that, and make no guarantee whatsoever
that the indexing will be the same); if they're different in size,
you'd need to rewrite that entire part of the function changing all
the TILE_FOO constants to something more mapTile_Foo-like. (I'm not
even going to contemplate the idea of using two _different_
user-defined tilesets, one for the map and one for inventory; this
would require adding another bitmap to the mswin_nhwindow_app struct,
and code for maintaining it. Rather you than me.)

[I am mostly talking through my hat here; I've never built NH on a
Windows machine, and have no great familiarity with the win/win32
code. But this looks to be the area you'd want to be fiddling with.]

